     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose entirely.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
